# Vault

Shared memory between mino and his coding agents. Plain markdown; Obsidian is
only the viewer. Agents read and write these files directly.

## How it works

`AGENTS.md` in this folder is the one file every agent session loads
(`~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md` is a symlink to it). It holds the rules and an index:
one line per topic, pointing at a note here. Agents read a note only when the
task touches it, and update the note (not AGENTS.md) when something changes.

| Path | What | Written by |
|---|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | Rules + index. Keep it short; it is paid for in every session. | mino, agents (index lines only) |
| `machine/` | This laptop: system, mango, login screen, power, network. | agents |
| `tools/` | Tools and helpers set up on this machine. | agents |
| `projects/` | One note per project or group of projects. metvas is the exception: its memory lives in the repo at `~/Projects/metvas/.memory/` (moved out 2026-11-12). | both |
| `reference/` | Longer reference material (the desktop PC, repo setup checklist). | both |
| `lessons.md` | Why the rules exist: the incidents and measurements behind them. | agents |
| `open-threads.md` | Unfinished work to pick up later. | agents |
| `todos.md` | mino's todo list, managed by `~/bin/todo`. | mino |
| `claude-memory/` | Legacy: Claude Code's auto-memory from Aug-Oct 2026. Frozen. | - |

Agent skills (procedures with their own trigger, loaded on demand) live in
`~/.pi/agent/skills/`: pib, delegation, pptx-maker, gmail, hallmark, web-search, pdf, xlsx.

## Conventions

- A note says what is true **now** and how to check it. Dated history goes at the bottom.
- Absolute dates, never "last week".
- If a note names a file or flag, verify it still exists before trusting it.
- `[[wikilinks]]` are fine; they are Obsidian's own syntax.
